+# VitaCheat NG 0.14.5
+
+Focused correctness fixes on the 0.14.4 baseline.
+
+## Executor and code generation
+
+- B200 requires a currently published module/segment. An unavailable selection stops the cheat before following memory accesses instead of using a zero or stale base.
+- Memory-map enumeration invalidates previous segment bases and presence before publishing the new map. Relative selectors remain relative when invalidated, preventing accidental absolute fallback.
+- Legacy pointer generation rejects U64/I64/F64. Two independent pointer-write sequences could resolve different objects between the low and high DWORDs. U8/U16/U32 pointer generation and fixed-address 64-bit generation remain supported.
+
+## Discovery
+
+- Manual generation, readiness policy and codegen all reject signatures awaiting relocation/revalidation. Restored AoB addresses cannot become generated absolute cheats while PENDING.
+- Periodic pointer revalidation uses a persistent round-robin cursor and a host-testable selector. Each pass still validates at most two paths. Empty lists, removals, sorting and relocation merges are handled without retaining stale candidate pointers.
+- Generated cheats remain OFF; persistence wire v3 and v2 compatibility remain unchanged.
+
+## Validation
+
+- The existing 56 host test executables pass, including new regressions within `vitacode`, `codegen` and `resolver_regressions`.
+- All 56 also pass with ASan/UBSan (`detect_leaks=0` in the traced local environment).
+- GitHub Actions verifies normal host, sanitizer and CTest Release gates before building real ARM plugins and the installer with a pinned official VitaSDK 2026.08 snapshot and taiHEN package.
+- ARM build status and artifact checksums are recorded separately after the workflow completes. Hardware validation remains pending.
+
+## Scope and remaining kernel work
+
+This revision does not change the kernel syscall ABI or claim K-06/K-07 complete. Own-SUPRX forced-write exclusion, kernel initialization diagnostics and lifecycle hardware checks remain separate work. The 0.14.4 hardware gate is still outstanding; no console validation is inferred from a successful build.
