+# VitaCheat NG 0.14.5 — hardware validation
+
+Use plugins and VPK produced by a successful build of this source commit. Verify SHA256SUMS and install/reboot normally.
+
+Repeat the storage, overlay, recovery-L and process-isolation checks in `HARDWARE_TEST_0.14.4.md`; those pending baseline checks still apply.
+
+## Regression checks
+
+1. With a purpose-built reversible diagnostic, select a B200 module/segment absent from the current map. The cheat must stop without reading or writing the following operand. Valid module/segment selections must still work.
+2. Repeat mission → loading → hub → mission. Removed segment bases must not remain usable after enumeration.
+3. Generate pointer cheats for 8/16/32-bit values and verify their normal behavior. Attempt U64/I64/F64 pointer generation: it must fail without adding a cheat. Fixed-address 64-bit generation remains available with its existing two-write behavior.
+4. Restore a previously persisted AoB candidate and press R while its signature is PENDING. Generation must be refused with a revalidation message. After unique relocation and live reread, any generated cheat must refer to the current target and start OFF.
+5. Track at least three eligible pointer paths between loading transitions. Periodic validation must eventually visit each path; a failing third path must lose CONFIRMED status. Repeat after sorting or removal of candidates.
+
+K-06 invalid-address testing still requires a dedicated safe diagnostic and protected saves. K-06 own-image exclusion and K-07 initialization status are not implemented by this revision.
